From 645052a836b5e2290216cf33eb29a817b41ee87e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:45:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] fix(trace): follow a membership's failure through S \cap
 T and S \ T to the set that fails

SetCapValue.member and SetDiffValue.member ask their first set, then,
where it holds the value, their second, and each lazy set the failure
passes through adds its source to the fingerprint stack. The evaluator
of failures followed a failure through a union and a filter but not
through an intersection or a difference, nor into a nested product
that fails on a value that isn't a tuple, so it left out the frames of
the sets inside. An equality with a lazy intersection or difference
enumerates it (`toSetEnum`), testing its first set's elements in its
second, whose failure now adds that set's frames too. 4 runs of the
upstream conformance suite that printed too few frames now match.
